{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And I heard a certain holy one</b> — like \"many of all peoples\" [i.e., a singular used with indefinite force]." "<b>To a certain one, an unknown one</b> — a compound word, for Daniel did not know his name at first. פלמוני is from the root פלאי, and אלמוני is from the root אלם. Now Daniel abbreviated and spoke as one speaking a riddle." "<b>And the meaning of \"the daily\"</b> — it is \"and from it the daily was removed.\" He sought to know how many days it would stand." "<b>And [it will be] given</b> — it is תנתן." "<b>And the sanctuary</b> — the place of His sanctuary." "<b>And the host</b> — \"and some of the host fell to the ground, and behold it is trampled\" — and it trampled them."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:32.214487551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}